					"path": "src/app.ts",
					"line": 79,
					"severity": "P3",
					"title": "`no_form` after a solver call is logged as zero attempts",
					"text": "🟢 **P3** · advisory\n\n**`no_form` after a solver call is logged as zero attempts**\n\n`reachedSolver` treats every `solveReason === \"no_form\"` as \"solver never called\". `no_form` is also returned when the pre-submit live recheck fails after a token was already obtained, for example a field added while the solver runs, which the existing test suite covers. In that case the solver call and its budget are spent, but the done log reports `attempts: undefined` and `challengeType: undefined`. Downstream dashboard cost accounting will undercount those attempts. A separate reason for the post-solve recheck, or a flag set once the solver is actually invoked, would make this accurate.\n\n<!-- ai-review:fp=bug|src/app.ts|3641d4d00f5be4ee.0 -->\n<!-- ai-review:advisory -->"
				}
			]
		}
